 "sensor": {
  "name": "WISE W1",
  "platform": "WISE (NASA/JPL), 525 km Sun-synchronous polar orbit",
  "band_nm": [
   2754.0,
   3872.0
  ],
  "notes": "HgCdTe 1024 x 1024 array, 18 um pixels, sample-up-the-ramp readout (no charge transfer: no smear, no CTI). Learned from 150 All-Sky W1 L1b int frames (qual_frame 10, Moon over 15 deg away), spread evenly in time over 2010-01-07 to 2010-08-06. Masked (NaN) pixels, 1.2% per frame, were filled before learning: isolated ones with the 5 x 5 median, saturated star cores with the brightest neighbour. Gain: header DEBGAIN 3.75 e-/DN (photon transfer over 305 high-latitude frames: 3.66). Read noise 11.4 e-, the noise floor of that photon transfer, given to the learner in the RDNOISE card: the 150 frames hold no pairs close in time. Spacecraft states at exposure start from JPL Horizons (-163). W1 saturates near magnitude 8: stars brighter than about Gaia G 9 come out fainter than the zeropoint and colour term predict."
 },
